     The trivial encryption is the same on all platforms, and it hasn't
changed since it was first introduced (I don't recall which version,
offhand--probably 3.2.0 or possibly even 3.1.0).  It is context sensitive
based on the start of the text; if the input string is missing the first
character or has an extra character inserted, the result would end up
being gibberish like was mentioned in the first post.  That might happen
if there was some problem in nethack's makedefs or dlb utilities--but no
problems have been reported for either of them in quite a long time--or
maybe if the machine had a disk or memory error.

     Feeding that gibberish back through the encryption/decryption code
(which uses the same transformation for both directions) might yield a
clue.  But I don't think that I'm going to bother....


